<section class="page-hero page-hero-simple about-hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">ABOUT THIS PROJECT</span><h1>A bigger way<br><em>to learn fruit.</em></h1><p>Fruit Atlas is an educational directory built to connect fruit names with botanical identity, regional diversity, flavour, growing context, food use and post-harvest care.</p></div><div class="simple-hero-side"><span class="big-serif-mark">FA</span><span class="side-rule"></span><p>Explore · compare<br>understand · grow</p></div></section>
<section class="section-block"><div class="section-heading-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">INSIDE THE CATALOGUE</span><h2>A catalogue with clear profile types</h2><p>The Atlas is designed for exploration first, with profile labels that tell you what kind of entry you are reading.</p></div></div><div class="catalogue-type-grid"><article><span class="type-kicker">BOTANICAL IDENTITY</span><h3>Species profiles</h3><p>Core fruit profiles with a botanical name, broad origin note, fruit group and general food and growing context.</p></article><article><span class="type-kicker">CULTIVATED DIVERSITY</span><h3>Named cultivar entries</h3><p>Curated named selections linked to a fruit species. Cultivar performance varies by provenance, climate and growing practice.</p></article><article><span class="type-kicker">FIELD OBSERVATIONS</span><h3>Fruit-form guides</h3><p>Editorial profiles about traits such as ripening, flesh colour, harvest, cooking and growing context. These are not presented as registered cultivar names.</p></article></div><div class="data-method-note"><strong>How to read the catalogue</strong><p>Fruit Atlas is a broad educational index—not a claim that every fruit form is independently taxonomically verified or every named cultivar has a complete breeder record.</p></div></section>
<section class="section-block about-method"><div class="section-heading-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">HOW TO USE THE ATLAS</span><h2>Use it to explore, then verify locally.</h2><p>Follow the learning library for in-depth articles on fruit chemistry, biology, ecology and horticulture.</p><a class="outline-link" href="/fruit-science">Explore fruit chemistry & biology ↗</a></div></div><div class="plain-two-column"><div><h3>Names and taxonomy</h3><p>Common names vary across countries and languages, and some names refer to more than one plant. Scientific names are included to help distinguish closely related fruits; taxonomy can change as botanical research develops.</p></div><div><h3>Nutrition and benefits</h3><p>Descriptions focus on general food context. Exact nutrient values are not inferred from colour or taste, and the Atlas avoids claiming that a fruit prevents or treats disease. Use a relevant food-composition database for specific quantities.</p></div><div><h3>Growing and seasons</h3><p>Origin notes and season descriptions are broad. For planting or harvest decisions, confirm climate suitability, pollination, maturity and local regulations with a regional horticultural source.</p></div><div><h3>Images</h3><p>Photos use online image URLs and attempt to find a more specific Wikipedia article image where available. Internet access is needed for those images; the catalogue and pages are served by the local Node.js app.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section-block source-links-section"><div class="section-heading-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">FURTHER READING</span><h2>Useful reference directions</h2><p>For in-depth research, confirm the facts with botanical, horticultural and food-composition references.</p></div></div><div class="quick-link-grid"><a href="https://www.fruitandnutlist.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><strong>Fruit & Nut Cultivars Database</strong><span>Cultivar names, synonyms and horticultural register information</span><b>↗</b></a><a href="https://www.fao.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><strong>Food and Agriculture Organization</strong><span>Crop production, agriculture and food systems</span><b>↗</b></a><a href="https://www.gbif.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><strong>Global Biodiversity Information Facility</strong><span>Species names and biodiversity occurrence records</span><b>↗</b></a><a href="https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><strong>USDA FoodData Central</strong><span>Food-composition and nutrition information</span><b>↗</b></a></div></section>
